@ 46.14 - Pre-Slavic Vowel Changes
# citation: Macska “PIE *a and *o with their variants have merged in the Balto-Slavic period; below they’re written both as *a.”
	e:[+long] > æ
	en an > ẽ ã
	ej > i
	ew > ju
	i > ı̆:[ə?]
	ı̆:[ə?] > {e,a} (strong)/∅ (weak) “in modern languages”
	i:[+long] > i
	a a:[+long] > o a
	aj > {æ₂,i₂} “(reduced)”
	aw > u
	u > ŭ:[ɤ?]
	ŭ:[ɤ?] > {e,o,ɤ,a} (strong)/∅ (weak) “in modern languages”
	u:[+long] > ɨ